<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan 10-yr T$30 bln bond yield at 5.654 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan 10-yr T$30 bln bond yield at 5.654 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's central bank, on behalf of the Finance Ministry, auctioned T$30 billion in 10-year government construction bonds on Friday with an average yield of 5.654 percent.  </p>
<p>The range of the bids was between 5.625 and 5.675 percent, a central bank official said.</p>
<p>The coupon rate on the bonds was set at 6.90 percent. Total demand was T$65.66 billion, the official said.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
